      "Subject-Verb Agreement (Concord): Verb must agree in number and person with true subject: singular subjects take singular verbs; compound subjects joined by 'and' take plural verbs; phrases like 'as well as', 'along with', and 'in addition to' do not alter subject number; collective nouns take singular verbs when acting as a single unit.",
