      "Common Syntactic Errors: Misplaced Modifiers (modifiers separated from the word they modify, creating absurd meanings); Dangling Modifiers (participial phrase lacking a grammatical subject to modify: 'Walking into the lab, the experiment exploded'); Comma Splices (joining two independent clauses with only a comma, corrected using semicolon or coordinating conjunction); Run-on Sentences.",
